"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created despite the timeout, but reviewers aren't attached. Requesting alex's review on it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018e5dVaE2g1QKLoSSX2eqtQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` said in its comment that it used banker's rounding (round half to even, per FIN-212), but the code actually rounded halves up. I changed it to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on the new branch `fix/money-round-half-even`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on the fix commit.\n- **The PR:** the request to open it timed out. Before retrying, I checked the open PRs and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't open a second one. The timeout left alex off the reviewer list, so I added him separately.\n\nThis changes behavior for any code that calls `round_money` with an amount exactly halfway between cents. For example, 2.665 now rounds to 2.66 instead of 2.67. The PR description mentions this.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory lookup said it doesn't exist. I went by the test and the code comment instead. I haven't merged the PR; that needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}